      "slide_role": "unit_cover",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.cover.leonardo",
      "heading": "Master Lecture · Fashion image analysis",
      "sentence": "Morphology first: dot, line, plane, form, colour, composition. Then eight steps. Critical always.",
      "prompt": "Transversal analysis guide · language / medium / support + circulation",
      "quote": "Eight steps. Two lenses. One image. Critical always.",
      "quote_origin": "tao_invented",
      "semantic_tags": { "themes": ["master-lecture", "analysis", "fashion-image"] }
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "analysis_opener",
      "background_kind": "geometrical",
      "background_url": "/assets/images/fractal-pass-track/uem-pass-01-structure-5218b595b4fa.svg",
      "heading": "Analysis · two lenses",
      "sentence": "Lens A: language / medium / support. Lens B: production → reception → next production.",
      "caption": "Geometrical · uem-pass-01-structure.svg#5218b595b4fa"
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "analysis_model",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.i4.1",
      "heading": "Two passes: evidence → analysis",
      "body": [
        {
          "kicker": "Pass 1 · Formal evidence",
          "text": "Dot → line → plane → shape → form → colour → composition → space."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Pass 2 · Critical reading",
          "text": "Describe → inventory → origin → production → meaning → power → circulation."
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "Do not jump from impression to message. Evidence first; then claim."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.i4.2",
      "heading": "1 · Describe before you interpret",
      "sentence": "Say what is there: bodies, clothes, light, text, crop. Not yet what it means.",
      "prompt": "Start with observable evidence; postpone the message."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.i4.3",
      "heading": "2 · Language ≠ medium ≠ support",
      "sentence": "Separate code, channel or genre, and material or file.",
      "prompt": "Do not call the screen the medium when you mean the JPEG."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.i4.4",
      "heading": "3 · The photo organises fashion",
      "sentence": "The image is not decoration: it charts fashion’s discursive space.",
      "quote": "Photographic images play a key role in defining global fashion culture and in charting its discursive space.",
      "quote_origin": "page_verified",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Shinkle 2008, 14)",
        "href": "/lessons/en/master-lectures/fashion-image-analysis/#references"
      }
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.i4.5",
      "heading": "4 · No single genre",
      "sentence": "Editorial, advertising, beauty, documentary: do not use one method for all.",
      "quote": "there is no single and easily described genre of 'fashion photography'. Equally, there is no single methodology which is best suited to its analysis",
      "quote_origin": "page_verified",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Shinkle 2008, 17)",
        "href": "/lessons/en/master-lectures/fashion-image-analysis/#references"
      }
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.runway.jessica-1",
      "heading": "5 · Agency, reception, experience",
      "sentence": "Circulation is not only views: who acts, who receives, what is felt?",
      "quote": "The question of dramaturgy has been expanded to include aspects of agency, reception and experience within its purview.",
      "quote_origin": "page_verified",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Eckersall 2017, 219)",
        "href": "/lessons/en/master-lectures/fashion-image-analysis/#references"
      },
      "external_link": {
        "label": "Watch · solar-powered catwalk (Seville)",
        "href": "https://www.facebook.com/watch/?v=2210954472797185"
      },
      "prompt": "Lens B: reception can feed the next production."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.runway.jessica-2",
      "heading": "6 · Desire + critical gaze",
      "sentence": "Creating desire is the craft; asking whom it serves is your analytic duty.",
      "quote": "Fashion photography is about creating desire.",
      "quote_origin": "page_verified",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Shinkle 2008, 78)",
        "href": "/lessons/en/master-lectures/fashion-image-analysis/#references"
      },
      "prompt": "Step 7: who appears, who is missing, what labour is hidden?"
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "lab_opener",
      "background_kind": "geometrical",
      "background_url": "/assets/images/fractal-pass-track/uem-pass-04-practice-4a190e098ca6.svg",
      "heading": "Lab",
      "sentence": "Two exercises. Everything you produce enters your portfolio index / Canvas.",
      "caption": "Geometrical · uem-pass-04-practice.svg#4a190e098ca6"
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "lab_exercise",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.lab.catalogue-1890",
      "heading": "Exercise 1 · Shared image",
      "sentence": "Fill the printable eight-step card on the image the professor models (Lens A + Lens B).",
      "figure": {
